// RUN: check
// COMPILE-FAIL
// EXPECT-EXIT: 65

// Regression: writing through an index path (`arr[i] = ...`) while `arr` is
// borrowed used to slip past the borrow checker entirely, because
// check_index_assign never called check_referent_access on the base object.
// The borrow is established through a `&int[]` call argument, which is the
// only lvalue position where the parser currently accepts a bare `&expr`
// (a standalone `&arr;` statement does not parse as a borrow today).

void hold(&int[] x) { return; }

int main() {
  int[] arr = [1, 2, 3];
  hold(&arr);
  arr[0] = 9;
  return 0;
}
